# Automa Coding Rules

## 1. Cấu trúc Thư mục (Folder Structure)

### Sơ đồ cấu trúc chính:

```
automa/
├── src/
│   ├── background/           # Service Worker (Manifest V3)
│   │   ├── index.js         # Entry point cho background script
│   │   ├── BackgroundEventsListeners.js
│   │   ├── BackgroundWorkflowUtils.js
│   │   └── BackgroundWebSocket.js
│   ├── content/             # Content Scripts
│   │   ├── index.js         # Main content script
│   │   ├── blocksHandler/   # Block execution handlers
│   │   └── elementSelector/ # Element selection utilities
│   ├── popup/               # Extension Popup UI
│   │   ├── App.vue
│   │   ├── index.js
│   │   └── pages/
│   ├── newtab/              # Dashboard UI (New Tab)
│   ├── components/          # Vue Components
│   │   ├── ui/             # UI Components (UiButton, UiInput, etc.)
│   │   ├── popup/          # Popup-specific components
│   │   └── newtab/         # Dashboard components
│   ├── stores/             # Pinia Stores
│   │   ├── workflow.js     # Workflow management
│   │   ├── user.js         # User data
│   │   └── main.js         # Main settings
│   ├── workflowEngine/     # Core Workflow Engine
│   │   ├── WorkflowManager.js    # Singleton workflow manager
│   │   ├── WorkflowEngine.js     # Main engine class
│   │   ├── WorkflowWorker.js     # Worker for block execution
│   │   └── blocksHandler/        # Block handlers
│   ├── utils/              # Utility functions
│   │   ├── message.js      # Message passing system
│   │   ├── backendApi.js   # Backend API calls
│   │   └── screenshotManager.js
│   ├── service/            # Services
│   │   └── browser-api/    # Browser API abstraction
│   ├── db/                 # Database (Dexie)
│   ├── lib/                # Third-party libraries
│   └── locales/            # Internationalization
├── manifest.chrome.json    # Chrome manifest
├── manifest.firefox.json   # Firefox manifest
└── webpack.config.js       # Build configuration
```

### Mô tả các thư mục chính:

**Background Script (`src/background/`)**:

- Chạy trong service worker context (Manifest V3)
- Xử lý events từ browser (tabs, alarms, commands)
- Quản lý workflow execution và WebSocket connections
- Không có DOM access, chỉ có API access

**Content Scripts (`src/content/`)**:

- Chạy trong context của web pages
- Thực thi các blocks trên trang web
- Có access đến DOM và page context
- Giao tiếp với background qua message passing

**Popup (`src/popup/`)**:

- UI nhỏ cho extension popup
- Sử dụng Vue 3 với Composition API
- Kích thước cố định: 350x500px

**New Tab Dashboard (`src/newtab/`)**:

- Giao diện chính của extension
- Workflow editor và management
- Sử dụng Vue Flow cho visual workflow builder

**Workflow Engine (`src/workflowEngine/`)**:

- Core logic cho workflow execution
- WorkflowManager: Singleton quản lý workflows
- WorkflowEngine: Engine chính xử lý workflow
- WorkflowWorker: Worker thực thi từng block

## 2. Quy tắc Code Vue Components

### 2.1 Cấu trúc Component

```vue
<template>
  <!-- Template với Tailwind CSS classes -->
  <div class="ui-component relative">
    <slot name="header" />
    <div class="content">
      <slot />
    </div>
  </div>
</template>

<script setup>
// Sử dụng Composition API
import { ref, computed, onMounted } from 'vue';
import { useComponentId } from '@/composable/componentId';

// Props definition
const props = defineProps({
  modelValue: {
    type: [String, Number, Object],
    default: '',
  },
  disabled: {
    type: Boolean,
    default: false,
  },
});

// Emits definition
const emit = defineEmits(['update:modelValue', 'change']);

// Component logic
const componentId = useComponentId('ui-component');
</script>

<style scoped>
/* Component-specific styles */
</style>
```

### 2.2 Naming Conventions

- **Component files**: PascalCase (e.g., `UiButton.vue`, `WorkflowEditor.vue`)
- **Props**: camelCase (e.g., `modelValue`, `isDisabled`)
- **Events**: kebab-case (e.g., `@update:model-value`)
- **CSS classes**: Tailwind utility classes, custom classes với prefix `ui-`

### 2.3 UI Component Patterns

- Sử dụng `v-bind="$attrs"` để forward attributes
- Implement `v-model` với `modelValue` prop và `update:modelValue` event
- Sử dụng slots cho customization (prepend, append, label)
- Component ID generation với `useComponentId` composable

### 2.4 State Management

- Sử dụng Pinia stores thay vì Vuex
- Store files trong `src/stores/`
- Naming: `use[Name]Store` (e.g., `useWorkflowStore`)

## 3. Giao tiếp qua Event Listeners

### 3.1 Message Passing System

```javascript
// Sử dụng MessageListener class
import { MessageListener, sendMessage } from '@/utils/message';

// Tạo listener
const message = new MessageListener('background');

// Đăng ký handler
message.on('workflow:execute', async (workflowData, sender) => {
  // Xử lý message
  return result;
});

// Gửi message
await sendMessage('workflow:execute', data, 'background');
```

### 3.2 Event Naming Convention

- Format: `[module]:[action]` (e.g., `workflow:execute`, `browser-api:call`)
- Prefix theo context: `background`, `content`, `popup`, `newtab`
- Response events: `[action]:response`

### 3.3 Cross-Context Communication

```javascript
// Background -> Content Script
await browser.tabs.sendMessage(tabId, {
  type: 'automa:execute-block',
  blockData: data,
});

// Content Script -> Background
const result = await sendMessage('workflow:execute', data, 'background');

// Popup -> Background
await sendMessage('open:dashboard', '/workflows', 'background');
```

### 3.4 Event Handler Patterns

```javascript
// Async handlers với error handling
message.on('api:call', async (data, sender) => {
  try {
    const result = await apiCall(data);
    return { success: true, data: result };
  } catch (error) {
    console.error('API call failed:', error);
    return { success: false, error: error.message };
  }
});

// Conditional handlers
message.on('workflow:execute', (data, sender) => {
  if (!data.workflowId) {
    throw new Error('Workflow ID is required');
  }
  return executeWorkflow(data);
});
```

## 4. Luồng Workflow Execution

### 4.1 Workflow Lifecycle

```
1. Trigger Event
   ↓
2. WorkflowManager.execute()
   ↓
3. WorkflowEngine.init()
   ↓
4. WorkflowWorker.executeBlock()
   ↓
5. Block Handler Execution
   ↓
6. Next Block or Completion
   ↓
7. WorkflowEngine.destroy()
```

### 4.2 Core Classes

**WorkflowManager** (Singleton):

```javascript
class WorkflowManager {
  static get instance() {
    if (!this.#_instance) this.#_instance = new WorkflowManager();
    return this.#_instance;
  }

  execute(workflowData, options) {
    const engine = new WorkflowEngine(workflowData, options);
    engine.init();
    return engine;
  }
}
```

**WorkflowEngine**:

```javascript
class WorkflowEngine {
  constructor(workflow, { states, logger, blocksHandler, options }) {
    this.workflow = workflow;
    this.states = states;
    this.logger = logger;
    this.blocksHandler = blocksHandler;
    this.workers = new Map();
  }

  async init() {
    // Initialize workflow state
    // Setup connections map
    // Start execution from trigger block
  }
}
```

**WorkflowWorker**:

```javascript
class WorkflowWorker {
  async executeBlock(block, execParam = {}) {
    // Execute individual block
    // Handle errors and retries
    // Move to next block
  }
}
```

### 4.3 Block Execution Pattern

```javascript
// Block handler structure
async function blockHandler(blockData, { refData, prevBlock, ...execParam }) {
  try {
    // Block execution logic
    const result = await performAction(blockData);

    return {
      data: result,
      nextBlockId: this.getBlockConnections(block.id),
      status: 'success',
    };
  } catch (error) {
    // Error handling
    return {
      data: error.data || '',
      nextBlockId: this.getBlockConnections(block.id, 'fallback'),
      status: 'error',
    };
  }
}
```

### 4.4 Error Handling Strategy

- **Block Level**: Retry mechanism với configurable retry times
- **Workflow Level**: Stop, continue, hoặc restart workflow
- **Global Level**: Notification và logging

### 4.5 State Management

- **Workflow States**: Stored in `WorkflowState` class
- **Reference Data**: Variables, table data, global data
- **Logging**: Structured logging với context data

## 5. Coding Standards

### 5.1 JavaScript/ES6+

- Sử dụng ES6+ features (async/await, destructuring, modules)
- Prefer `const` over `let`, avoid `var`
- Use template literals cho string interpolation
- Destructure objects và arrays khi có thể

### 5.2 Vue 3 Best Practices

- Sử dụng Composition API với `<script setup>`
- Reactive data với `ref()` và `reactive()`
- Computed properties cho derived state
- Lifecycle hooks: `onMounted`, `onUnmounted`, etc.

### 5.3 Error Handling

```javascript
// Consistent error handling pattern
try {
  const result = await operation();
  return { success: true, data: result };
} catch (error) {
  console.error('Operation failed:', error);
  return { success: false, error: error.message };
}
```

### 5.4 Async/Await Patterns

```javascript
// Prefer async/await over Promises
async function processData() {
  try {
    const data = await fetchData();
    const processed = await processData(data);
    return processed;
  } catch (error) {
    throw new Error(`Processing failed: ${error.message}`);
  }
}
```

### 5.5 File Organization

- Một class/component per file
- Export default cho main export
- Named exports cho utilities
- Index files cho re-exports

### 5.6 Comments và Documentation

```javascript
/**
 * Executes a workflow block with error handling and retry logic
 * @param {Object} block - Block configuration
 * @param {Object} execParam - Execution parameters
 * @returns {Promise<Object>} Execution result
 */
async function executeBlock(block, execParam = {}) {
  // Implementation
}
```

## 6. Testing và Debugging

### 6.1 Debug Mode

- Enable debug mode trong workflow settings
- Console logging với structured data
- Screenshot capture on errors
- Breakpoint support trong testing mode

### 6.2 Error Reporting

- Structured error objects với context
- Error categorization (network, DOM, logic)
- User-friendly error messages
- Automatic error reporting to backend

### 6.3 Performance Monitoring

- Block execution timing
- Memory usage tracking
- Workflow completion metrics
- Resource cleanup verification

## 7. Security Considerations

### 7.1 Content Security Policy (CSP)

- Handle CSP violations gracefully
- Use debugger API khi scripting bị block
- Sanitize user inputs
- Validate external data

### 7.2 Permission Management

- Request permissions only when needed
- Handle permission denials gracefully
- Provide clear permission explanations
- Implement permission fallbacks

### 7.3 Data Protection

- Encrypt sensitive data trong storage
- Validate data trước khi process
- Sanitize outputs
- Implement data retention policies

## 8. Performance Guidelines

### 8.1 Memory Management

- Clean up event listeners
- Remove unused references
- Use WeakMap cho temporary data
- Monitor memory usage

### 8.2 Execution Optimization

- Batch operations khi có thể
- Use requestIdleCallback cho non-critical tasks
- Implement proper caching
- Optimize DOM operations

### 8.3 Bundle Size

- Tree-shake unused code
- Lazy load components
- Optimize images và assets
- Monitor bundle size

